{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/discontiguousslice\/enumerated()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence of pairs ("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" represents a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents an element of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice\/enumerated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence","text":"EnumeratedSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of pairs enumerating the sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example enumerates the characters of the string “Swift” and prints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each character along with its place in the string.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for (n, c) in \"Swift\".enumerated() {","    print(\"\\(n): '\\(c)'\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"0: 'S'\"","\/\/ Prints \"1: 'w'\"","\/\/ Prints \"2: 'i'\"","\/\/ Prints \"3: 'f'\"","\/\/ Prints \"4: 't'\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you enumerate a collection, the integer part of each pair is a counter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the enumeration, but is not necessarily the index of the paired value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These counters can be used as indices only in instances of zero-based,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer-indexed collections, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContiguousArray"},{"type":"text","text":". For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other collections the counters may be out of range or of the wrong type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to use as an index. To iterate over the elements of a collection with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zip(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example iterates over the indices and elements of a set, building a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list consisting of indices of names with five or fewer letters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let names: Set = [\"Sofia\", \"Camilla\", \"Martina\", \"Mateo\", \"Nicolás\"]","var shorterIndices: [Set<String>.Index] = []","for (i, name) in zip(names.indices, names) {","    if name.count <= 5 {","        shorterIndices.append(i)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now that the "},{"code":"shorterIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array holds the indices of the shorter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"names"},{"text":" set, you can use those indices to access elements in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the set."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for i in shorterIndices {","    print(names[i])","}","\/\/ Prints \"Sofia\"","\/\/ Prints \"Mateo\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"enumerated()","extendedModule":"Swift","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:STsE10enumerateds18EnumeratedSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s18DiscontiguousSliceV","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10"},{"beta":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"beta":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/DiscontiguousSlice":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A collection wrapper that provides access to the elements of a collection,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indexed by a set of indices.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"DiscontiguousSlice","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscontiguousSlice","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscontiguousSlice","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/discontiguousslice"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/EnumeratedSequence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/enumeratedsequence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EnumeratedSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EnumeratedSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EnumeratedSequence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An enumeration of the elements of a sequence or collection."}]},"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}],"type":"image","alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background.","identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/DiscontiguousSlice/enumerated()":{"title":"enumerated()","abstract":[{"text":"Returns a sequence of pairs (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emph